# Underwater-mode camera property.
#
# CAUTION, deliberate deviation from stock:
# stock declares vendor_oplus_underwater_prop with
#   property_type, system_property_type, system_public_property_type
# (vendor_sepolicy.cil:1068-1070) even though it lives in the VENDOR policy and
# is labelled by vendor_property_contexts:474.  That combination only survives
# because OPlus turns off BUILD_BROKEN_TREBLE_SYSPROP_NEVERALLOW-style checks.
# On a stock-neverallow EvolutionX build, declaring a system_property_type from
# a vendor sepolicy dir trips the treble sysprop neverallows.
#
# Use the vendor-owned form instead; the app is a coredomain, so it needs the
# property to be readable+settable across the treble boundary:
vendor_internal_prop(vendor_oplus_underwater_prop)
#
# If that turns out to be too strict at runtime (coredomain writing a
# vendor_internal_prop), switch to:
#   vendor_public_prop(vendor_oplus_underwater_prop)
# and keep the property_contexts entry as-is.
